  candidate: Yep, there are a couple of a11y bugs here, and they line up w/ the tester log.

1) **Enter on a suggestion is not doing a “select” action.**
In `LabelPicker.tsx` the suggestions are just `<div onClick=...>` items, not real buttons/listbox options. There is no `onKeyDown` on the options, and the input only handles ArrowUp/ArrowDown:

```tsx
onKeyDown={(e) => {
  if (e.key === "ArrowDown") ...
  if (e.key === "ArrowUp") ...
}}
```

So when keyboard user presses **Enter**, nothing in `LabelPicker` selects the highlighted suggestion. In the dialog, Enter falls through to the form submit behavior in `AddLabelsDialog.tsx`:

```tsx
<form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
```

That calls `saveLabels(itemIds, chosen);` and then closes the modal. If no label was added to `chosen`, it just closes. That matches “pressing Enter on a suggestion closes the dialog without adding the label.”

2) **The dialog is not focus-managed, so closing sends you back to page top.**
In `Modal.tsx` there is no focus trap, no initial focus on the dialog, and no restore-focus-to-trigger behavior. It just portals markup and closes on Escape/click:

```tsx
return createPortal(..., document.body)
```

So when the modal closes, focus likely returns to `body` / the browser default, which is why the tester ends up at the top of the page. The log probably shows focus landing on the page header/skip link or losing virtual cursor position after close.

3) **For screen readers, the picker is not exposed as a proper widget.**
The suggestions list is plain divs with no roles like `listbox`/`option`, no `aria-activedescendant`, and the input has no label, just placeholder text. SR users will hear something like an edit field and then a bunch of unlabeled clickable divs, not a navigable autocomplete. Also the close control is an icon-only `div` in `Modal.tsx`:

```tsx
<div className="icon-button" onClick={onClose}>
  <svg aria-hidden="true" ... />
</div>
```

That is not keyboard-accessible and not announced as a button.

So short version: **Enter submits/closes instead of selecting**, and **focus/semantics are missing**, so both keyboard and SR users get a broken modal flow and bad focus return.

