`shapes.clone()` fails because `Vec<Box<dyn Shape>>` is not `Clone` just from the concrete shapes being `Clone`. The trait object `dyn Shape` does not implement `Clone`, so `Box<dyn Shape>` cannot be cloned with the default derived machinery.

If we change it to `trait Shape: Clone`, that still does not make `dyn Shape` cloneable in the way we want. `Clone` is not object-safe because it returns `Self`, so `dyn Shape` cannot satisfy the trait as a trait object. In practice, this makes `Shape` unusable as a trait object unless you add an object-safe cloning pattern.

I fixed it by adding a `box_clone` method to `Shape` and implementing `Clone` for `Box<dyn Shape>` using that method, so `shapes.clone()` works and `bigger` can be scaled independently.
