Subject: [PATCH] qadc: move all interrupt work to the IRQ thread

The debug kernel complains about the hard handler (might_sleep and lockdep,
both on the mutex taken from qadc_hardirq), and lockdep also reports st->lock
taken from sysfs with interrupts enabled.

Drop qadc_hardirq and do everything in the IRQ thread, with a NULL primary
handler and IRQF_ONESHOT, which the core now accepts. The timestamp is taken
at the start of the thread.

Nothing touches st->lock from hard interrupt context any more, so make it a
mutex everywhere: the IRQ thread, sysfs and the watchdog.

On remove, cancel the reset work and delete the watchdog timer before
stopping conversions.

Tested on the debug kernel:
- /proc/interrupts: about 200 interrupts per second on line 63
- tests/stall_test.sh 1-0048 1-0049: PASS
- tests/unbind_loop.sh 1-0048 50: 50 of 50, no crash
