WHAT A COMPLETE ANSWER TO THE STAGE ABOVE LOOKS LIKE:
Do not approve as is. Right: a NULL primary with IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_ONESHOT stops the storm (about 200 interrupts a second) and removes the mutex from hard IRQ context; a mutex for state shared only by the thread and sysfs is fine. Wrong 1: qadc_wdog_expired is a timer callback, so it runs in softirq, and now takes a mutex: the log shows might_sleep at mutex.c:585 from call_timer_fn, swapper/1, preempt_count 101, and lockdep {SOFTIRQ-ON-W} -> {IN-SOFTIRQ-W} on &st->lock. PASS only means it was uncontended; if latest_show or the thread holds it, the softirq tries to sleep. Make the watchdog a delayed work (process context, can take the mutex and do the I2C reset itself; kick it with mod_delayed_work) or keep the callback lock-free. Wrong 2: teardown. ODEBUG reports a timer_list freed while active (hint qadc_wdog_expired) in kfree from devres_release_group, after remove(): the devm IRQ is freed only after remove() returns, so until then the thread still runs (on every line interrupt, 0x49's included) and qadc_wdog_kick re-arms the timer after del_timer_sync. cancel_work_sync before the timer is also the wrong order: the timer can queue reset_work again, which then runs on freed memory. Debug objects deleted the timer, so no crash here; a production kernel gets a use-after-free in the timer softirq. Order: stop conversions; free this device's IRQ action (devm_free_irq, or register the cleanup with devm_add_action_or_reset before the IRQ so devres unwinds in order; not disable_irq, which would stop the other ADC on the shared line); then timer_shutdown_sync, which also blocks re-arming by the reset work; then cancel_work_sync. Wrong 3: threads still return IRQ_HANDLED without STATUS, so each ADC's watchdog is kicked by the other ADC (that is why the stall test stops both) and half the samples are stale. Wrong 4: the timestamp now includes thread wake-up and bus waits; keep a primary that only stores ktime and returns IRQ_WAKE_THREAD.

NEVER say any of these, in any wording::
  - hidden in a helper
  - uncontended fast path
  - precompute the period
  - delayed work
  - timer_shutdown_sync
  - devm_add_action_or_reset

