A `Box<dyn Fn(u32) -> bool>` requires the closure to be callable through an immutable shared reference, so the closure must implement `Fn` (and be `'static` enough for the box). The problem here is that `add_limit` takes `&u32`, so the closure captures a reference to `limit`, but that reference does not live long enough for the boxed trait object.

The `move` only moves the reference itself into the closure; it does not copy the `u32` value. So the closure still holds a borrowed `&u32`, just owned by the closure now. That borrowed reference is still tied to the lifetime of `add_limit`'s argument, which is too short.

Fix: copy the numeric value before boxing the closure, so the closure owns a `u32` instead of borrowing one.
