The smallest fix to `run_twice` is to change the bound to `FnMut` and make the parameter mutable:

```rust
fn run_twice<F: FnMut()>(mut f: F) {
    f();
    f();
}
```

If someone changed the bound to `impl FnOnce()` instead, then the error would move to the second call inside `run_twice`. `FnOnce` only guarantees the closure can be called one time, because it may consume captured values when called. So `f();` is allowed once, but the second `f();` becomes the problem.
