--- README.md ---
# adc-capture

Linux platform driver for the ADC capture block (IP version 1.2) in the FPGA
fabric. The block samples 4 ADC channels at 16 bits and 5 MS/s each, packs the
samples into 64 KiB frames and writes the frames to DDR with its own descriptor
DMA engine. User space reads whole frames from `/dev/adc-capture0`.

## Board

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| CPU | 4 x Cortex-A53 (arm64) at 1.2 GHz, 32 KiB L1 D-cache per core, 1 MiB shared L2, 64-byte lines |
| DDR | 2 GiB at bus address 0x0000_0000 (no IOMMU, bus address = physical address) |
| Fabric to DDR | the block's AXI master goes through a high-performance port that is **not** cache-coherent: CPU caches are not snooped (no `dma-coherent` in the node) |
| Fabric clock | `fclk0`, 250 MHz, clocks the block (`s_axi_aclk`) |
| Kernel | 6.12.40, arm64 defconfig plus the board options |
| Interrupt | GIC SPI 89, level high |

Data rate: 4 channels x 2 bytes x 5 MS/s = 40 MB/s, one 65536-byte frame every
1.6384 ms (about 610 frames per second).

## Register map

The register file is 0x000 to 0x113 inside a 4 KiB window. Base address in the
fabric address map: 0xa001_0000.

| Offset | Name | Access | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0x000 | ID | RO | [31:16] major, [15:0] minor. 0x0001_0002 for v1.2 |
| 0x004 | CTRL | RW | bit 0 ENABLE, bit 1 TEST_PATTERN, bit 31 RESET (self-clearing; clears FRAME_CNT, DESC_HEAD, DESC_TAIL) |
| 0x008 | STATUS | RW1C | bit 0 FRAME_DONE, bit 1 DESC_ERR, bit 2 OVERRUN; bit 8 BUSY (RO) |
| 0x00c | IRQ_EN | RW | same bits as STATUS[2:0] |
| 0x010 | FRAME_BYTES | RW | bytes per frame, multiple of 64 |
| 0x014 | CLKDIV | RW | ADC sample clock = 250 MHz / (CLKDIV + 1) |
| 0x018 | FRAME_CNT | RO | frames completed since ENABLE |
| 0x100 | DESC_BASE | RW | bus address of the descriptor ring (32 bits, 16-byte aligned) |
| 0x104 | DESC_COUNT | RW | descriptors in the ring |
| 0x108 | DESC_HEAD | RO | descriptors completed since RESET (free-running) |
| 0x10c | DESC_TAIL | RW | descriptors handed to the block since RESET (free-running, written by the driver) |
| 0x110 | DESC_ERR_IDX | RO | ring index of the descriptor that raised DESC_ERR |

## Descriptor DMA engine

Each descriptor is 16 bytes, little endian (`struct cap_desc` in `capture_regs.h`):

| Word | Field |
|---|---|
| 0 | ctrl: [31] OWN (set by the driver, cleared by the block when the frame is done), [23:0] buffer length |
| 1 | status (written by the block): [31] DONE, [30] ERR, [23:0] bytes written |
| 2 | addr: buffer bus address (32 bits) |
| 3 | seq (written by the block): frame number |

- **Prefetch.** When DESC_TAIL moves, the block reads the newly handed-over
  descriptors from DDR at once, into an 8-entry descriptor cache. It reads
  each descriptor once, with one 16-byte AXI read.
- A prefetched descriptor without OWN is a descriptor error: the block sets
  DESC_ERR and DESC_ERR_IDX, aborts the frame in progress, drops its
  descriptor cache and stops. Writing DESC_TAIL again restarts it from DESC_HEAD.
- When a frame is complete the block writes status and seq, clears OWN in
  ctrl, waits for the write responses, increments DESC_HEAD, then raises
  FRAME_DONE.
- `seq` counts frames of the sample stream from ENABLE, including frames the
  block could not store (aborted, or no descriptor ready: OVERRUN), so a lost
  frame shows as a gap in `seq`.
- The engine writes whole 64-byte bursts wherever the buffer address allows;
  buffer addresses need only 4-byte alignment.

## Test pattern

With CTRL.TEST_PATTERN set, the block replaces the ADC samples with a counter:
word i (0 to 16383) of frame n is `(n & 0xffff) << 16 | i`. `tools/capcheck`
checks every word of every frame against it.

## Build and load

```
make KDIR=/path/to/linux-6.12.40 ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu-
insmod adc_capture.ko test_pattern=1
make -C tools
./tools/capcheck -n 20000 /dev/adc-capture0
```

The block runs from probe to remove. Frames that nobody reads are dropped
once the 32-frame read pool is full.

## Files

| File | What |
|---|---|
| `capture_main.c` | probe, remove, device tree match |
| `capture_dma.c` | buffers, descriptor ring, start and stop, interrupt handlers |
| `capture_cdev.c` | `/dev/adc-capture0`, the read pool |
| `capture.h`, `capture_regs.h` | driver structures, register map |
| `uapi/adc_capture.h` | the record header read() returns |
| `dts/adc-capture.dtsi` | the node the board .dts includes |
| `bindings/lab,adc-capture.yaml` | device tree binding |
| `tools/capcheck.c` | test-pattern checker |

