It won’t compile because `bump` mutates `count`, so it only implements `FnMut`, not `Fn`. The current `run_twice` asks for a shared, non-mutating callable, but this closure needs mutable access to the captured state.

Smallest fix on `run_twice` is to take `FnMut` and make the parameter mutable:

```rust
fn run_twice<F: FnMut()>(mut f: F) {
    f();
    f();
}
```

If the bound were changed to `FnOnce()` instead, the error would move to the second call inside `run_twice`. A `FnOnce` can be called only one time because it may consume the captured values on that first call, so `f(); f();` would be the problem. The `run_twice(bump)` call would then be accepted, but the body would fail on the second invocation.
