--- README.md ---
# admin-console

Internal console for the order operations staff: the orders list, and the shared
settings that drive it (page size, default filter, refund approval limit, a banner).

- Next.js 16.3 (App Router), React 19.3, TypeScript 7.0. Cache Components is not enabled.
- All data comes from the admin REST API at `ADMIN_API_URL`. The console calls it with
  a service token, `ADMIN_API_TOKEN`.
- Sign-in is handled by the company SSO, which sets the `sid` session cookie.
  `GET /me` on the API, called with the session id as the bearer token, returns the
  signed-in user: `{ userId, team, role }`.
- Roles: `editor` can change settings, `viewer` can only read them.
- The settings form is generated from `config/settings.schema.json`. The values live in
  the API (`GET /settings`, `PUT /settings`).

## Layout

- `app/layout.tsx`: the shell and the account badge (`app/account-provider.tsx`)
- `app/settings/`: the settings page, its form and its save action
- `app/orders/page.tsx`: the orders list
- `app/api/account/route.ts`: the signed-in user, for the badge
- `lib/`: calls to the admin API
- `proxy.ts`: the sign-in redirect

## Run locally

```
export ADMIN_API_URL=http://localhost:4000 ADMIN_API_TOKEN=...
npm ci
npm run build
npm start
```

## Deploy

The pipeline runs `next build` in a clean checkout once per release and ships the image to
three containers that run `next start` behind the load balancer (round robin, no sticky
sessions). Each container has its own `.next` directory.

