--- README.md ---
# qadc

Out-of-tree Linux driver for the board's two 4-channel, 16-bit ADCs on I2C
bus 1 (400 kHz), at addresses 0x48 and 0x49.

## Board

- SoC: i.MX7 Dual (2 x Cortex-A7, 32-bit ARMv7).
- Kernel: 6.12.34, `CONFIG_PREEMPT=y`, `HZ=100`. The GPIO bank interrupt
  is handled on CPU0.
- Each ADC has an open-drain, active-low RDY output. The two RDY outputs are
  wired together to GPIO1_IO17 with a 10 kohm pull-up (`dts/`).

## ADC registers

| Addr | Name | Content |
|---|---|---|
| 0x00 | STATUS | bit 0 DRDY: a new result is in DATA; bit 1 OVR: a result was overwritten before it was read |
| 0x01 | CONFIG | bits 2:0 rate: 0 off, 1 25 Hz, 2 50 Hz, 3 100 Hz, 4 250 Hz, 5 500 Hz, 6 1000 Hz; bit 7 CONT: continuous conversions |
| 0x02 to 0x09 | DATA | CH0 to CH3, 16-bit big-endian |
| 0x0F | ID | reads 0x5A |

- The register address auto-increments, so a 9-byte read from 0x00 returns
  STATUS followed by DATA.
- RDY goes low when DRDY is set. It stays low until the result is read: a
  read that includes the last DATA byte (0x09) clears DRDY and releases RDY
  at its STOP. Reading STATUS alone does not release RDY.
- A new result overwrites DATA whether or not the previous one was read.
- At power-up CONFIG is 0x00 (no conversions).

## Driver

| File | What it does |
|---|---|
| `qadc-core.c` | probe and remove, interrupt handlers, watchdog |
| `qadc-sysfs.c` | sysfs attributes |
| `qadc.h` | registers, `struct qadc` |

- Default rate: 100 Hz on each ADC.
- On each RDY interrupt the driver reads DATA (8 bytes) over I2C and stores
  the sample, with the interrupt's timestamp, in a 256-entry ring.
- Watchdog: when no conversion arrives for 8 periods, the driver restarts the
  ADC (CONFIG written to 0, then back to the configured rate).

## sysfs

Per ADC, in `/sys/bus/i2c/devices/1-0048/` and `/sys/bus/i2c/devices/1-0049/`:

| Attribute | Mode | Content |
|---|---|---|
| `latest` | r | newest sample: `<timestamp ns> <ch0> <ch1> <ch2> <ch3>` |
| `stats` | r | `samples`, `irqs` and `resets` counters |
| `odr` | rw | conversion rate in Hz: 0, 25, 50, 100, 250, 500 or 1000 |

## Build and load

    make KDIR=/path/to/linux-6.12 ARCH=arm CROSS_COMPILE=arm-linux-gnueabihf-

The module is loaded at boot from `/etc/modules-load.d/qadc.conf`.

## Tools and tests

| Script | What it does |
|---|---|
| `tools/qadc-mon.sh` | reads `latest` from both ADCs every 100 ms (runs on the device in production) |
| `tests/stall_test.sh <dev>...` | stops conversions on the listed ADCs with `i2cset`, waits 500 ms, checks that `resets` went up |
| `tests/unbind_loop.sh <dev> <n>` | unbinds and rebinds the driver from one ADC, n times |

