`Box<dyn Fn(u32) -> bool>` requires the closure to be callable after it has been stored, which in practice means the captured values must have a lifetime compatible with the boxed trait object. In `p3.rs`, `add_limit` takes `limit: &u32`, and the closure is stored in `self.rules`, so it cannot keep a borrow of `limit` unless that borrow is proven to live long enough. The `move` only moves the reference itself into the closure; it does not copy the `u32` value, so the closure still contains a borrowed reference and the borrow ends when `add_limit` returns.

Fix: copy the `u32` value out first, then move that copied value into the closure.
