`shapes.clone()` fails because `Vec<Box<dyn Shape>>` can only be cloned if the trait object type `dyn Shape` is cloneable. Even though `Square` and `Circle` derive `Clone`, a `Box<dyn Shape>` does not automatically know how to clone the erased concrete value behind it.

If we changed it to `trait Shape: Clone`, that would make `Shape` not object-safe. `Clone` requires `Self: Sized` for `clone`, so `dyn Shape` would stop being usable as a trait object, and `Box<dyn Shape>` would no longer compile.

To make this work, I added an object-safe cloning helper to the trait and implemented `Clone` for `Box<dyn Shape>`, so the vector can be cloned. Then `bigger` is scaled independently and `shapes` stays unchanged.
