So uncovered shapes are: `Level(100)` and `Pulse { width: 0..=10, repeat: false }`.

(2) Guarded `Pulse` arm count for nothing because guards do not make a pattern exhaustive in Rust. `Signal::Pulse { width, repeat: false } if *width > 10` only matches a subset of that pattern. Compiler ignores the guard for exhaustiveness checking, so the whole `repeat: false` branch still needs an unguarded arm.

